<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;I&gt;&amp;gt; there is no "use strict" in Awk or Bourne-family shells&lt;/I&gt;&lt;P&gt;

In larger bash scripts (which should be turned to Perl scripts, really) I always start with
&lt;c&gt;
set -eu
&lt;/c&gt;&lt;P&gt;

and put all code into a &lt;c&gt;main()&lt;/c&gt; function, so that I can declare all variables with &lt;c&gt;local&lt;/c&gt;. It's not as strict as [doc://strict], but it helps a lot.&lt;P&gt;



&lt;!-- Node text goes above. Div tags should contain sig only --&gt;
&lt;div class="pmsig"&gt;&lt;div class="pmsig-832495"&gt;
&lt;c&gt;map{substr$_-&gt;[0],$_-&gt;[1]||0,1}[\*||{},3],[[]],[ref qr-1,-,-1],[{}],[sub{}^*ARGV,3]&lt;/c&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;!-- Wiki2Monks {"version":1.16} --&gt;</doctext>
